-- N4 grammar, part one: forms the language builds on.
--
-- Same rules as 009: the JLPT point LIST is a fact about the exam, every word
-- of the prose is written for this app, and nothing here is imported. Points
-- ship `published` so the level is usable, at status 'in-review' until a human
-- signs each one off.
--
-- Seven points a standard N4 list carries are deliberately absent from these
-- two files: dake, nagara, shika-nai, sugiru, ta-koto-ga-aru, toki and tsumori.
-- All seven are already taught at N5 in 011, and (language_id, slug) is unique,
-- so restating them here would be seven rows that silently never insert.
--
-- sort_index continues from N5 (which ends at 49) at 100, so the two levels
-- never collide and the ordering stays stable if N5 grows.

ON CONFLICT (language_id, slug) DO NOTHING;
